  "response_text": "The initial value of the Main Stack Pointer (MSP) is important in determining a valid Process Stack Pointer (PSP) because we need a starting address to anchor the PSP calculation to a specific memory region in the RAM. Assuming we have already obtained the value of MSP_INIT_VAL, we calculated PSP_val by subtracting 0x400 from it. This is because the main stack is 0x400 bytes in size and since stacks grow downward, the memory space it occupies lies below MSP_INIT_VAL. To allocate a new region below the main stack for the process stack, we subtract 0x400 to move further down in memory.\\n",
